# Xv6 and Unix Utilities Lab 🐧

This lab is part of my journey through **MIT 6.1810 (Operating Systems)**, where I explored **xv6**, a re-implementation of Unix Version 6 for modern RISC-V processors. The goal of this lab was to implement several Unix utilities in xv6, such as `sleep`, `pingpong`, `primes`, `find`, and `xargs`. These tasks helped me understand system calls, processes, pipes, and file systems in xv6.

